  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Good morning! My name is Sarah Williams. It's an honour to be here and to share with you the story of how music has had an {impact} on my life.",
      "cn": "早上好，我叫莎拉·威廉姆斯。很荣幸来到这里与大家分享音乐是如何影响我的人生的。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Have you ever faced a time when things looked dark and you had no hope at all? Two years ago, I was told I had a serious {disease} which was difficult to {cure}. My body ached all the time and {thus} I thought I didn't have much longer to live. I was very afraid and I felt so alone and discouraged. Then one day, I had to go through a two-hour medical {treatment}. The doctor wanted me to relax, so he had me listen to some music, and one of the songs was \"Happy\". The song made me feel so much better that from then on I began to listen to music all the time. John A. Logan said, \"Music is the medicine of the mind.\" And it's true. Music helped me recover.",
      "cn": "你有没有过这样的经历：眼前一片漆黑，而你感到毫无希望？两年前，我被告知患上了一种难以治愈的重病。我的身体一直在疼痛，因此我以为自己时日无多了。我非常害怕，感到无比孤独和沮丧。后来有一天，我不得不接受两个小时的治疗。医生想让我放松，于是让我听了一些音乐，其中一首歌叫《快乐》。这首歌让我感觉好多了，从那时起，我开始一直听音乐。约翰·洛根说过：\"音乐是心灵的良药。\"的确如此，音乐帮助我康复了。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Music gave me happiness. When I listened to music, it made my spirits fly like a kite in the wind. Music gave me strength and brought me {relief}. It was the rock I leant on to become strong and to get through those hard times. {Moreover}, music gave me hope and a sense of {satisfaction}. It became my best friend. It spoke words of encouragement to the deepest part of my {being}.",
      "cn": "音乐带给我快乐。当我听音乐时，我的精神像风中的风筝一样飞翔。音乐给我力量，让我解脱。它是我所依靠的岩石，让我变得坚强，度过那些艰难的岁月。此外，音乐给了我希望和满足感。它成了我最好的朋友。它在我的内心深处说着鼓励的话语。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Of course, I hope none of you have to go through the same kind of suffering that I did. At the same time, we all go through {various} periods when we feel sad or alone. During those times, music can help you in the same way that it helped me. I hope all of you will {somehow} begin to treasure music and make it a part of your life.",
      "cn": "当然，我希望你们都不要经历我所遭受的那种痛苦。与此同时，我们都会经历感到悲伤或孤独的不同时期。在那些时候，音乐可以像帮助我一样帮助你。我希望你们所有人都能以某种方式开始珍视音乐，并让它成为你生活的一部分。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Thank you!",
      "cn": "谢谢大家！"
    }
  ],
